 "final_message": "All twelve items are done and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20133:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate` and `flags_in_window` now follow sections 1\u20133. The old window summed `days + 1` entries.\n- **Items 4\u20135:** `parse_transcript_log` maps `flagged` to `1`\u2192True, `0`\u2192False and empty\u2192None, and skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines. Errors say `line N`, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 6\u20137:** `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last record for each id. `daily_flag_counts` returns one entry per day in the range, with zeros for empty days.\n- **Item 8:** `monitor_summary` rounds the rate to 3 places and counts only non-empty groups.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added tests for `None` counting as not flagged and for the last duplicate id winning.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `flags_in_window` entry is fixed and `daily_flag_counts` is added. I also reworded the entries for `dedupe_transcripts` and `longest_alert_streak` to match the spec.\n- **Item 12:** In the rest of the package, `top_flagged_groups` was in `report.py` and wrong. I moved it to `metrics.py`, where its tie-break by name and its exclusion of empty groups now work. `flag_rate_by_group` returns `None` for empty groups, with keys sorted. `longest_alert_streak` never reset its run on a zero day, which is fixed.\n\n`report.py` re-exports `top_flagged_groups`, so existing imports from there still work.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` field other than `1`, `0` or empty, such as `yes`. I made that raise `ValueError` with `line N`, rather than guess a value.",
